### Phase 1 — Existing project/setup inspection `[x]`

- **Objective:** Confirm the real repository layout, stack, and working defaults so later phases extend this project instead of replacing it.
- **Main tasks:**
  - Inventory root files (`package.json`, `next.config.ts`, `tsconfig.json`, `app/`, `public/`).
  - Confirm Next.js 16 / React 19 / Tailwind v4 / App Router.
  - List what is **absent** (backend, DB, auth, tests, Docker).
  - Document structure rules: no `frontend/` folder; no source under `public/`.
- **Files/modules likely involved:** `package.json`, `package-lock.json`, `app/layout.tsx`, `app/page.tsx`, `app/globals.css`, `next.config.ts`, `tsconfig.json`, `eslint.config.mjs`, `public/*`, `PROMPTS.md`, `.cursorrules`.
- **Dependencies:** None (first phase).
- **Verification/checkpoint:** `npm run dev` still serves the default Next.js page; `npm run lint` runs.
- **Definition of done:** Written inventory of current vs intended architecture; no feature code added.

---

### Phase 2 — Frontend foundation `[x]`

- **Objective:** Establish IRAS frontend conventions on the existing `app/` tree without building full product pages yet.
- **Main tasks:**
  - Keep create-next-app structure; add only foundational pieces: env example for API URL, typed API client stub, shared layout shell (header/footer placeholders), path aliases already `@/*`.
  - Configure CORS-ready `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL` (or equivalent) pointing at future Spring Boot.
  - Add UI primitives only when needed (prefer existing Tailwind; add Shadcn later if a later phase requires it).
  - Do not move the app into `frontend/` or `public/`.
- **Files/modules likely involved:** `app/layout.tsx`, `app/globals.css`, `app/page.tsx`, new `lib/` or `components/` at repo root (alongside `app/`, not under `public/`), `.env.example`, `next.config.ts`.
- **Dependencies:** Phase 1.
- **Verification/checkpoint:** App still builds; placeholder layout renders; API base URL is documented; no backend required yet.
- **Definition of done:** Stable Next.js foundation, shared layout/types, env contract for the API, default Next branding can remain until Phase 8/19.

---

### Phase 3 — Backend foundation `[x]`

- **Objective:** Add Spring Boot at `backend/` (sibling of `app/`) with base configuration, without replacing the Next.js app.
- **Main tasks:**
  - Create Spring Boot project (Maven or Gradle) with web, validation, actuator.
  - Application properties / profiles (`dev`, `test`).
  - CORS for the Next.js origin.
  - Health endpoint; package structure (`config`, `common`, `security` stubs).
  - PostgreSQL + Flyway + JPA starters wired but schema can wait for Phase 4.
- **Files/modules likely involved:** `backend/pom.xml` or `backend/build.gradle`, `backend/src/main/java/**`, `backend/src/main/resources/application*.yml`, `backend/.gitignore`.
- **Dependencies:** Phase 1 (structure rules); Phase 2 (known frontend origin/port).
- **Verification/checkpoint:** Backend starts; `/actuator/health` (or equivalent) returns UP; Next.js still starts independently.
- **Definition of done:** Runnable Spring Boot service next to existing Next.js app; no business entities required yet.

---

### Phase 4 — Database setup and schema `[x]`

- **Objective:** PostgreSQL + Flyway migrations + JPA entities/relationships for IRAS (users, addresses, categories, products, images, inventory, wishlist, cart, orders, payments).
- **Main tasks:**
  - Local PostgreSQL (Docker optional here; full compose is Phase 23).
  - Flyway versioned SQL for tables, indexes, constraints, enums/status columns.
  - JPA entities and repositories matching migrations (source of truth = Flyway).
  - Seed strategy for later catalog/admin work (dev-only).
- **Files/modules likely involved:** `backend/src/main/resources/db/migration/V*.sql`, `backend/**/domain/**`, `backend/**/repository/**`, `application.yml` datasource settings.
- **Dependencies:** Phase 3.
- **Verification/checkpoint:** App starts against empty DB and Flyway applies cleanly; schema matches entity graph; no data-loss migrations.
- **Definition of done:** Repeatable schema in Git; entities compile; repositories can be injected.

---

### Phase 5 — Authentication `[ ]`

- **Objective:** Signup/login, OTP verification, JWT access tokens, HttpOnly refresh cookies, role-aware protected routes (customer vs admin).
- **Main tasks:**
  - Auth APIs: register, request/verify OTP, login, refresh, logout.
  - Password hashing; JWT access token; refresh token store + HttpOnly Secure cookie.
  - Spring Security filters; CORS credentials.
  - Next.js auth pages and session handling (cookies via same-site/proxy or documented cross-origin cookie setup). Do **not** default to NextAuth/Stripe from old notes unless a later prompt overrides `PROMPTS.md`.
- **Files/modules likely involved:** `backend/**/auth/**`, `backend/**/security/**`, `app/(auth)/*` or `app/login`, `app/signup`, `lib/auth.ts`, middleware if used.
- **Dependencies:** Phases 2–4.
- **Verification/checkpoint:** Register → OTP → login → access protected API → refresh → logout; unauthenticated access denied.
- **Definition of done:** Working customer auth with JWT + refresh cookie; admin role flag exists even if admin UI is later.

---

### Phase 6 — User profile and address management `[ ]`

- **Objective:** Authenticated users can view/update profile and CRUD shipping addresses.
- **Main tasks:**
  - Profile GET/PATCH (name, phone, email rules).
  - Address CRUD; default address; validation (required fields, PIN, etc.).
  - Frontend account/profile and address screens using Phase 2 layout.
- **Files/modules likely involved:** `backend/**/user/**`, `backend/**/address/**`, `app/account/**` (or similar under `app/`), form components.
- **Dependencies:** Phase 5.
- **Verification/checkpoint:** Authenticated user updates profile and addresses; default address persists; other users cannot access these records.
- **Definition of done:** Profile + addresses APIs and UI complete for a logged-in customer.

